The first choice for engraving Elbereth is the wand of fire:  the
results are permanent, and there's no unfortunate side effect
(other than using one charge from the wand).

Second choice, if you don't have a wand of fire, is situational:
in some cases the wand of lightning is the second choice,
but in other cases a wand of digging (or an athame, if you've
got one) is better.

The wand of digging is abundantly available and has no real
side effects, but the engraving is not *entirely* permanent
(although it's MUCH better than writing in the dust with
your fingers).  An athame has similar results but doesn't
use up charges, so you can do it as often as you like.
There are also cases where you can use a hard gem or
ring, but that takes longer, so it's not good for emergencies.

The wand of lightning results in a permanent Elbereth
(like with the wand of fire) but blinds you in the process.
This can be better (than the athame or wand of digging)
in some situations, e.g., if you don't want the engraving
to ever fade because you intend to store a blessed potion
of water on it for emergencies.

In the early game, though, you usually don't have
anything like that to engrave with, so the only available
Elbereth is writing it in the dust with your fingers.  This
is MUCH harder to learn to use effectively.  If you're
anything like me doing it wrong will get you killed
several dozen times before you get the hang of it.

The other thing that has got me several times is
forgetting that a certain monster ignores Elbereth.


